Reports directly to the Board through the Board Audit and Risk Committee with a dotted line to the general manager. The main functions of the Role are to ensure that all risks within the business are identified, have owners and have mitigating controls in place, and to create an environment where risk and control are clearly understood and is taken seriously by all staff. Furthermore, the Internal Audit Manager is expected to play an important role in inputting the efficiency and effectiveness of the Bank.
